# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# task-rabbit-mcp configuration. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
# Every setting is read from the environment. There is no config file.
#
# The strict rules: TASK_RABBIT_URL and TASK_RABBIT_API_KEY must be set together
# or not at all, because a URL with no key can only ever mean "use a key I was
# never given"; and on a publicly-reachable listener, setting them also requires
# TASK_RABBIT_MCP_ALLOW_DEFAULT_INSTANCE=1, because a default instance is then
# served to every caller who names no instance of their own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL default jirrabit instance.
#
# Leave BOTH unset for a shared server: every call then names its own instance
# with the instanceUrl and apiKey tool arguments, which is what you want when
# several people connect to one task-rabbit-mcp to reach their own jirrabit.
#
# Set BOTH for a personal single-instance server, so calls can omit the
# arguments. Loopback and private addresses are fine here — it is the operator's
# own choice — but they are refused when a *caller* supplies them.
#
#   jirrabit in the same compose network:  http://web:8000
#   jirrabit on the host, containerised:   http://host.docker.internal:8000
#   jirrabit on a domain:                  https://jirrabit.example.com
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TASK_RABBIT_URL=
TASK_RABBIT_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host allowlist for caller-supplied instance URLs.
#
# Unset means any host that is not loopback or link-local, which is right for a
# trusted LAN. Set it for a published server: it is checked per call, and it is
# the control that stops this server being used to reach somebody else's
# network. Entries are exact, except that a leading dot matches a domain and its
# subdomains.
#
#   TASK_RABBIT_ALLOWED_HOSTS=jirrabit.example.com,.internal.example.com
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TASK_RABBIT_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transport. stdio is the default and the shape to prefer locally: the client
# spawns this process, so there is exactly one caller and it is the user.
#
# A containerised server is a service, so the image defaults to http. Binding to
# loopback and terminating TLS in a proxy is the shape to prefer there too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TASK_RABBIT_TRANSPORT=stdio
# TASK_RABBIT_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8083
# TASK_RABBIT_PATH=/mcp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repositories, and where their jirrabit project keys live.
#
# A JSON object mapping jirrabit project key to a local checkout:
#
#   TASK_RABBIT_REPOS={"WEB":"/home/you/code/web","OPS":"/home/you/code/ops"}
#
# Without this, a tool call works on the repository the agent is standing in, or
# whatever repoPath the call names. Set it when one person works across several
# checkouts and should not have to repeat the path on every call.
#
# Refused at start-up on a publicly-reachable listener: a published server that
# knows where your checkout lives, and can run its test suite, is remote code
# execution.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TASK_RABBIT_REPOS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where materialised attachments are written.
#
# Defaults to a directory under the system temp dir. Deliberately NOT inside the
# repository: an issue with screenshots on it would otherwise leave untracked
# files in `git status` that the agent then has to reason about, or worse, commit.
#
# Use an ABSOLUTE path. A relative one is resolved against the process's working
# directory, which in a container is `/`.
#
# The container image creates /tmp with mode 1777 at build time, so the default
# works there. Point this at a mounted volume to keep the files past the
# container's lifetime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TASK_RABBIT_WORKSPACE=/tmp/task-rabbit

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bounds for a single check run, in seconds. The default is generous because a
# full test suite is not fast; the point of a timeout is to stop a hung process,
# not to enforce a speed budget.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TASK_RABBIT_CHECK_TIMEOUT=600

# How much of a check's output to return, in bytes, per check. Enough to read a
# linter's findings, not enough to fill the model's context with a test log.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TASK_RABBIT_OUTPUT_LIMIT=8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maximum size of a single materialised attachment, in bytes. jirrabit caps
# attachments at 5 MB.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TASK_RABBIT_MAX_ATTACHMENT=5242880